/*!
\page page_stpsd StPsd

\brief Base class for Physics Summary Data (PSD) objects; extended by each Physics Working Group to store group-specific summary quantities in StEvent.

\section overview Overview

`StPsd` is the base class for Physics Summary Data objects in STAR. PSD objects are
physics-working-group-specific summary quantities computed during offline reconstruction and stored
persistently in \ref StEvent via the `StPsdCollection`. Each PWG subclasses `StPsd` and adds its
own physics quantities. The `mPwg` field identifies the owning PWG; `mId` distinguishes multiple
PSD types within a group. This mechanism allows lightweight, group-specific summaries to be
appended to the event record without modifying core \ref StEvent structures.

\section hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject
└── StObject
    └── StPsd
        └── (PWG-specific subclasses)
\endcode

\section datamembers Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StPwg` | `mPwg` | Physics Working Group identifier (e.g. `kStar`, `kAuAu`) |
| `Int_t` | `mId` | PWG-assigned PSD type identifier |

\section keymethods Key Methods

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| `StPwg pwg() const` | Returns the PWG identifier |
| `Int_t id() const` | Returns the PWG PSD type identifier |
| `void setPwg(StPwg pwg)` | Sets the PWG identifier |
| `void setId(int id)` | Sets the PSD type identifier |

\section example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
// Concrete subclass pattern:
// class MyPwgPsd : public StPsd {
//   float mJetEnergy {0.f};
// public:
//   MyPwgPsd() : StPsd(kMyPwg, 1) {}
//   float jetEnergy() const { return mJetEnergy; }
//   ClassDef(MyPwgPsd, 1)
// };

StPsdCollection* psdc = event->psdCollection();
if (psdc) {
    for (size_t i = 0; i < psdc->size(); ++i) {
        StPsd* psd = (*psdc)[i];
        if (psd->pwg() == kMyPwg && psd->id() == 1)
            cout << "jet E=" << static_cast<MyPwgPsd*>(psd)->jetEnergy() << endl;
    }
}
\endcode

\see StEvent
*/
